index=entra sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:azurediagnostics" ResourceProvider="MICROSOFT.KEYVAULT" Category="AuditEvent" OperationName="SecretGet" earliest=-14d latest=now
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` Detection (SPL): Bulk secret reads from Key Vault (credential harvesting) ```
``` Lab:             Contoso Health Identity Platform - Splunk second SIEM     ```
``` KQL twin:        lab/kql/keyvault-bulk-secret-read.kql                     ```
```                  (same logic, window and output columns)                  ```
``` -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` STAND-IN: Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL. DATA GAP, said plainly: neither ```
``` the live feed (feed-splunk-live.py) nor the replay                         ```
``` (ingest-from-loganalytics.sh) carries AzureDiagnostics today, so this      ```
``` search has no Key Vault rows to read. It runs and returns nothing until a  ```
``` feed sends the Key Vault AuditEvent rows with this sourcetype.             ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHAT IT CATCHES                                                             ```
```   Per caller (object id, else app id, else UPN - most callers are managed ```
```   identities with no UPN), in the last hour: successful SecretGet reads   ```
```   (HTTP 200) above max(20, 5 x its own hourly mean over the 335 hours     ```
```   before), or 20 or more refused reads (HTTP 403). Severity column: High  ```
```   when either signal covers 5 or more distinct secrets, else Medium.      ```
```   HTTP 404 (missing secret) and SecretList never count.                   ```
``` MITRE ATT&CK: T1555.006 Cloud Secrets Management Stores;                  ```
```               T1552.001 Credentials In Files.                             ```
```                                                                            ```
``` KQL -> SPL TRANSLATION                                                      ```
```   SecretGets / Baseline lets + join          -> one stats BY CallerId with ```
```                                               baseline and judge-hour sums ```
```   coalesce(oid, appid, tolower(upn))         -> coalesce(nullif(...))      ```
```   extract(/secrets/name, id_s)               -> rex on id_s                ```
```   make_set_if(SecretName, 200 or 403, 20)    -> values() + mvindex 0..19   ```
``` HONEST DIFFERENCE: dc() is exact; KQL dcount is an estimate (exact at      ```
``` these small numbers).                                                     ```
```                                                                            ```
``` SCHEDULE: PT1H / P14D, base severity Medium, throttled 1 h per caller.     ```
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` @stanza Contoso - Bulk secret reads from Key Vault ```
``` @conf description = One caller (keyed on object id, so managed identities count) read Key Vault secrets far above its own normal rate in the last hour, or had 20 or more reads refused. High across 5 or more secrets. KQL twin: lab/kql/keyvault-bulk-secret-read.kql ```
``` @conf disabled = 0 ```
``` @conf enableSched = 1 ```
``` @conf cron_schedule = 13 * * * * ```
``` @conf dispatch.earliest_time = -14d ```
``` @conf dispatch.latest_time = now ```
``` @conf counttype = number of events ```
``` @conf relation = greater than ```
``` @conf quantity = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.track = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.severity = 4 ```
``` @conf alert.expires = 7d ```
``` @conf alert.digest_mode = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.fields = CallerId,Severity ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.period = 1h ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_app = search ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_view = search ```
| eval CallerId=coalesce(nullif(identity_claim_oid_g, ""), nullif(identity_claim_appid_g, ""), nullif(lower(identity_claim_upn_s), ""), "(unknown)")
| eval Status=tonumber(httpStatusCode_d)
| rex field=id_s "/secrets/(?<SecretName>[^/?]+)"
| eval InJudge=if(_time>=relative_time(now(), "-1h"), 1, 0)
| eval BaseRead=if(InJudge==0 AND Status==200, 1, 0), JudgeRead=if(InJudge==1 AND Status==200, 1, 0), JudgeDeny=if(InJudge==1 AND Status==403, 1, 0)
| eval ReadSecret=if(JudgeRead==1, SecretName, null()), DenySecret=if(JudgeDeny==1, SecretName, null()), JudgeSecret=if(JudgeRead==1 OR JudgeDeny==1, SecretName, null())
| eval JudgeTime=if(InJudge==1, _time, null()), JudgeVault=if(InJudge==1, Resource, null()), JudgeVaultId=if(InJudge==1, ResourceId, null())
| eval JudgeOid=if(InJudge==1, nullif(identity_claim_oid_g, ""), null()), JudgeAppId=if(InJudge==1, nullif(identity_claim_appid_g, ""), null()), JudgeUpn=if(InJudge==1, nullif(identity_claim_upn_s, ""), null()), JudgeType=if(InJudge==1, nullif(identity_claim_idtyp_s, ""), null()), JudgeIp=if(InJudge==1, nullif(CallerIPAddress, ""), null())
| stats sum(BaseRead) AS BaselineReads, sum(JudgeRead) AS Reads, sum(JudgeDeny) AS Denied, dc(ReadSecret) AS Secrets, dc(DenySecret) AS DeniedSecrets, values(JudgeSecret) AS SecretNames, max(JudgeTime) AS LastEpoch, dc(JudgeVault) AS Vaults, values(JudgeVaultId) AS VaultIds, values(JudgeOid) AS Oids, values(JudgeAppId) AS AppIds, values(JudgeUpn) AS Upns, values(JudgeType) AS Types, values(JudgeIp) AS Ips BY CallerId
| where isnotnull(LastEpoch)
| eval HourlyMean=BaselineReads / 335
| eval ReadThreshold=max(20, HourlyMean * 5)
| eval BulkRead=if(Reads > ReadThreshold, "true", "false"), DeniedBurst=if(Denied >= 20, "true", "false")
| where BulkRead=="true" OR DeniedBurst=="true"
| eval Signal=case(BulkRead=="true" AND DeniedBurst=="true", "bulk read + denied burst", BulkRead=="true", "bulk read", true(), "denied burst")
| eval Severity=if((BulkRead=="true" AND Secrets >= 5) OR (DeniedBurst=="true" AND DeniedSecrets >= 5), "High", "Medium")
| eval SecretNames=mvindex(SecretNames, 0, 19)
| eval CallerObjectId=mvindex(Oids, 0), CallerAppId=mvindex(AppIds, 0), CallerUpn=mvindex(Upns, 0), CallerType=mvindex(Types, 0), CallerIp=mvindex(Ips, 0), VaultResourceId=mvindex(VaultIds, 0)
| eval TimeGenerated=strftime(LastEpoch, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%3N%z")
| sort 0 - LastEpoch
| table TimeGenerated, Severity, Signal, CallerId, CallerType, CallerUpn, CallerObjectId, CallerAppId, CallerIp, Reads, Secrets, Denied, DeniedSecrets, SecretNames, Vaults, VaultResourceId, BaselineReads, HourlyMean, ReadThreshold
